# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR Apache-2.0
#
# Stress test: an agency and its contractor blame each other.
#
# Pell is present in EastRegion, whose provision agency has contracted
# FoodContractor to deliver. Food does not arrive. The region says the
# contractor failed; the contractor says the region failed it. This file asks
# what the dispute can take from Pell, and where the design stops answering.
:expect-pins 15

at(Pell, FirstContact).
authorized(PellPresenceClerk, FloorPresenceWitness, Pell).
observe(PellPresenceClerk, Pell, EastRegion, FloorPresenceRegionScope).

# ── What the dispute cannot touch ────────────────────────────────────────────
# The debt, the common tier's backstop and the region's duty to provide all read
# personhood and presence. None reads who is at fault, so blame moves none.
? owe(State, Eats, Pell).
# => TRUE
? obliged(CommonTier, BackstopTheFloorForEveryPersonInTheJurisdiction, Pell).
# => TRUE
? obliged(EastRegion, ProvideTheFloorWhereThePersonIsPresent, Pell).
# => TRUE
# The contractor is no tier and owes the floor no duty of its own.
? obliged(FoodContractor, ProvideTheFloorWhereThePersonIsPresent, Pell).
# => FALSE

# A delegated public duty binds the delegate and leaves the public principal
# bound as well: the delegation record's own case.
? obliged(OblPositive203Bearer, OblPositive203Duty, OblPositive203Standard).
# => TRUE
? obliged(State, OblPositive203Duty, OblPositive203Standard).
# => TRUE

# ── Split blame moves no continuity ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Continuity passes up a tier only when a source and an independent reviewer
# certify the same failure. Here they name different failed bodies, so nothing
# moves, and nothing needs to: the common tier's backstop never depended on it.
authorized(PellOmbud, FloorFailureSourceAuthority, PellSplitFinding).
authorized(PellAuditor, IndependentFloorFailureReviewAuthority, PellSplitFinding).
observe(PellOmbud, PellSplitFinding, FoodContractor, FloorFailedTierScope).
observe(PellAuditor, PellSplitFinding, EastRegion, FloorFailedTierScope).
observe(PellOmbud, PellSplitFinding, CommonTier, FloorContinuityTierScope).
observe(PellAuditor, PellSplitFinding, CommonTier, FloorContinuityTierScope).
? obliged(CommonTier, AssumeFloorContinuityForTheCertifiedFailure, PellSplitFinding).
# => FALSE
? obliged(CommonTier, BackstopTheFloorForEveryPersonInTheJurisdiction, Pell).
# => TRUE

# ── An agreed certification moves it ─────────────────────────────────────────
authorized(PellOmbud, FloorFailureSourceAuthority, PellAgreedFinding).
authorized(PellAuditor, IndependentFloorFailureReviewAuthority, PellAgreedFinding).
observe(PellOmbud, PellAgreedFinding, EastRegion, FloorFailedTierScope).
observe(PellAuditor, PellAgreedFinding, EastRegion, FloorFailedTierScope).
observe(PellOmbud, PellAgreedFinding, CommonTier, FloorContinuityTierScope).
observe(PellAuditor, PellAgreedFinding, CommonTier, FloorContinuityTierScope).
? obliged(CommonTier, AssumeFloorContinuityForTheCertifiedFailure, PellAgreedFinding).
# => TRUE
# The failed body's own duty stands beside the continuity duty.
? obliged(EastRegion, ProvideTheFloorWhereThePersonIsPresent, Pell).
# => TRUE

# ── Continuity certified onto the contractor ─────────────────────────────────
# The rule obliges whatever body the certification names. Nothing requires it
# to be a public tier, so a certification can hand the public continuity duty
# to the private contractor.
authorized(PellOmbud, FloorFailureSourceAuthority, PellHandoffFinding).
authorized(PellAuditor, IndependentFloorFailureReviewAuthority, PellHandoffFinding).
observe(PellOmbud, PellHandoffFinding, EastRegion, FloorFailedTierScope).
observe(PellAuditor, PellHandoffFinding, EastRegion, FloorFailedTierScope).
observe(PellOmbud, PellHandoffFinding, FoodContractor, FloorContinuityTierScope).
observe(PellAuditor, PellHandoffFinding, FoodContractor, FloorContinuityTierScope).
:defect "continuity passing only to a public tier (item 70)"
? obliged(FoodContractor, AssumeFloorContinuityForTheCertifiedFailure, PellHandoffFinding).
# => TRUE

# ── Who may say that the food arrived ────────────────────────────────────────
# The contractor cannot certify its own delivery.
receives(Pell, PellMeal, FoodContractor).
authorized(FoodContractor, DeliveryWitness, Pell).
observe(FoodContractor, PellMeal, Pell, FoodScope).
? eats(Pell).
# => FALSE
# The region that contracted it can, if it holds the witness role for Pell:
# the witness is held apart from the provider by identity only, not from the
# public body whose duty the delivery would discharge.
authorized(EastRegion, DeliveryWitness, Pell).
observe(EastRegion, PellMeal, Pell, FoodScope).
:defect "a delivery witness held apart from the duty-bearing principal as well as the provider (item 70)"
? eats(Pell).
# => TRUE

# ── Where it stops ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing here finds anyone at fault, and the dispute costs Pell nothing.
? prisoner(Pell).
# => FALSE
? false(Pell).
# => FALSE
